uuid "8065c595-2459-5ec7-a994-35d5484d61c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-69727" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5}{4})=(\\frac{4}{3})+[]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\frac{5}{4}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $5$ and position $4$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{5}{4})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{5}{0}) &  & (\\frac{5}{1}) &  & (\\frac{5}{2}) &  & (\\frac{5}{3}) &  & (\\frac{5}{4}) &  & (\\frac{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{5}{4})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{5}{4})=(\\frac{4}{3})+(\\frac{4}{4})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{4}{4}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-69727/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69727"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer/id #uuid "52ee241a-fbec-5f9f-939c-dc21caea0f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" :answer/id #uuid "e03578b6-dc69-5311-9aec-dfb0cc870029" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "d5dd0728-2cda-54b7-bf15-9ebac07ed698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "ffac70b7-9f1d-51aa-aea3-27647526aa5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "ec2b6703-84d3-528c-8ad3-3a8dd69a44fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0bc7ce-f4e8-5b8f-8400-10dac4f6d174" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70313/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer-field/choices ["q-70313/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" "q-70313/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" "q-70313/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-70313/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-70313/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70313" :question/id #uuid "e84202b0-9543-596a-a3aa-3519e01fe1ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-70313" :question/problem "Determine the value of $(\\frac{7}{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{4}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{3!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70313/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70313"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610/selection/56079b7d9864bca8be4ed3956a02bbba59a88ffb217bad1dd02eff30e5113394" :answer/id #uuid "6df17955-e07c-53ef-afc4-0f590455e790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610/selection/fbed0a59c3aa72b3f138ce42d582b9feee4514be4be4d8305eb71bf3c81e623b" :answer/id #uuid "57a58c1e-7704-5fab-9054-2949065b61c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610/selection/3393d52de45673b50b889fdb548fc66aeb7dd8bae133db7e2497d4cde2a6c881" :answer/id #uuid "5d7295d9-88a6-5c92-b040-301e940d7e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610/selection/11a6e1da3f0c0e7a672dadefdfbb0ed8c12e0fe986e8a4baf598d5b68f8f67d3" :answer/id #uuid "763d5835-293a-5250-8926-2b2cc1867adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610/selection/a1f9f20fc8800ea90ba70c87425e47839cbca8ba08cc3eef35a65d0cffe3ef3c" :answer/id #uuid "185ff776-3b36-511e-94a8-0c06caa92d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d746608f-d1c9-5f00-bebe-de6d08c926e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113610/selection/11a6e1da3f0c0e7a672dadefdfbb0ed8c12e0fe986e8a4baf598d5b68f8f67d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-113610/selection/56079b7d9864bca8be4ed3956a02bbba59a88ffb217bad1dd02eff30e5113394" "q-113610/selection/fbed0a59c3aa72b3f138ce42d582b9feee4514be4be4d8305eb71bf3c81e623b" "q-113610/selection/3393d52de45673b50b889fdb548fc66aeb7dd8bae133db7e2497d4cde2a6c881" "q-113610/selection/11a6e1da3f0c0e7a672dadefdfbb0ed8c12e0fe986e8a4baf598d5b68f8f67d3" "q-113610/selection/a1f9f20fc8800ea90ba70c87425e47839cbca8ba08cc3eef35a65d0cffe3ef3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113610" :question/id #uuid "ca37ba0c-8a3a-5194-96ea-e828544c2875" :question/math-academy-id "q-113610" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{4}{2})=[]+(\\frac{3}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\frac{4}{2}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $4$ and position $2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{4}{2})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{4}{2})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{4}{2})=(\\frac{3}{1})+(\\frac{3}{2})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{3}{1}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113610/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113610"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113611/selection/14a7e8ee9c39c69988c7b8dc9dbde21761684641d1e30d6bd452d0ab05bc7313" :answer/id #uuid "a56d991f-fb6d-54a8-b60f-390d11048dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113611/selection/56079b7d9864bca8be4ed3956a02bbba59a88ffb217bad1dd02eff30e5113394" :answer/id #uuid "d975a7a0-24e7-5766-b197-2f78d8922a33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113611/selection/87735ab2df82b33e3fe549cf07da1a0df7e3064138a1901262acbdc61d4c0f29" :answer/id #uuid "aa62cb21-c956-5b7b-9c04-2b9d5151c317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{4}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113611/selection/0b72f753053845efa3a5a28e438ec76379e6c3fe5a11a9c799beb78310e7a49b" :answer/id #uuid "a60b26b4-2dcd-5dce-81a2-1047b9efc575" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{6}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113611/selection/0e17d0d94d34cbe3a0b5afb53daaa1c70fe450713a8d9494fda2220825058256" :answer/id #uuid "9420d7d7-995a-5587-9424-690adfd4a6ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113611/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d81e81b6-bc5a-5c7d-8841-255628cd8730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113611/selection/14a7e8ee9c39c69988c7b8dc9dbde21761684641d1e30d6bd452d0ab05bc7313" :answer-field/choices ["q-113611/selection/14a7e8ee9c39c69988c7b8dc9dbde21761684641d1e30d6bd452d0ab05bc7313" "q-113611/selection/56079b7d9864bca8be4ed3956a02bbba59a88ffb217bad1dd02eff30e5113394" "q-113611/selection/87735ab2df82b33e3fe549cf07da1a0df